course: dictionary
lesson: 6321
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one the writer means. The word mother is a good example. «Tigers have bright white spots on the backs of their black ears, which may help cubs follow their mother» is about a female tiger with cubs, not about your own mum.
explain: Ask yourself who or what the mother is in the sentence. In «Kneading... starts with kittens feeding from their mother», the mother is an animal that feeds her young. The clues in the sentence will show you which meaning fits.
explain: Mother can also be a verb, a doing word. To mother someone is to care for them, sometimes too much. If a story says an older sister «mothered» her little brother, she looked after him closely, the way a mum would.
fact: A mother is a woman who has a child. Your mother is your mum or mom.
fact: An animal mother is the female that has babies, like the mother bird.
fact: To mother someone means to care for them, sometimes too much.
fact: «Mother tongue» means your first language.
fact: Mother can be a noun (mother, mothers) or a verb (mother, mothers, mothered).
exercise: «Tigers have bright white spots on the backs of their black ears, which may help cubs follow their mother.» In this sentence, what is the mother? | A tiger's name at the zoo | A kind of white paint | *A female tiger that has cubs | A teacher at a school
exercise: «The older girl mothered her little brother all day.» What does mothered mean here? | Argued with him | Went to the shops | Forgot about him | *Cared for him closely, the way a mum would
exercise: «A seal pup alone on a beach is usually not lost: its mother may be fishing nearby.» Find and copy one word that means the seal that has the pup. | *mother | fishing | nearby | beach
test: What does «mother tongue» mean? | *Your first language | A dog's bark | A kind of cake | A song sung by a mum
test: «Dad's mother is Mum's mother-in-law.» What is Dad's mother to Mum? | Her daughter | Her sister | Her friend from school | *Her mother-in-law
exam: Which sentence uses mother as a verb? | «The mother cat had three kittens in the barn.» | *«She mothered the lost puppy until its owner came.» | «My mother is a nurse who works nights.» | «Mother Nature gives us rain and sun.»
